# 20. Key Takeaways

- Admission Controllers intercept Kubernetes API requests after authentication and authorization.
- Mutating admission can automatically change resource configurations.
- Validating admission enforces policies and rejects invalid requests.
- LimitRanger manages resource defaults.
- ResourceQuota controls namespace resource consumption.
- Pod Security Admission enforces Pod Security Standards.
- Kyverno provides Kubernetes-native policy management.
- Dynamic admission webhooks support custom validation and mutation.
- SecurityContext controls container runtime privileges.
- Admission policies improve consistency, security, and governance.

